## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies (148 packages added)

**2. Component Integration**
Modified: `src/App.jsx`
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react'`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component next to the existing `<Analytics />` component at the root level of the App component
- Placement follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

### Implementation Details

- **Framework:** React 19.2.7 with Vite 8.1.1
- **Documentation Source:** Latest official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart)
- **Package Manager:** npm (package-lock.json updated)
- **Integration Pattern:** Added alongside existing @vercel/analytics implementation

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ No new linting errors introduced (pre-existing error in solver.js is unrelated)
✅ Package-lock.json properly updated with new dependencies
✅ Component properly imported and integrated into the app structure

### Next Steps

To complete the Speed Insights setup:
1. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Speed Insights → Enable)
2. Deploy to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
3. Monitor performance metrics in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site

The integration will automatically create the required routes (`/_vercel/speed-insights/*`) on the next deployment.

### Notes

- The SpeedInsights component was placed at the same level as the Analytics component for consistency
- No additional configuration was needed for the React/Vite setup
- The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation exactly as specified
